---
// A Tuesday, honestly (design: Story). Seven moments, each "How it is" and
// "With doze", all rendered here; src/scripts/story-tuesday.ts flips them.
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---
<Page title="A Tuesday, honestly" current="none">
<div class="st st-s1" data-story>

  <section class="st-s2">
    <span class="st-eyebrow">A story you already know</span>
    <h1 class="st-h st-hero st-s3">A Tuesday, honestly.</h1>
    <p class="st-s4">You don't call it a mess. It's just how the day goes: the tabs, the ports, the fan, the setup doc nobody trusts. Step through it, then flip each moment to see it with doze.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="st-s5" aria-label="The day">
    <nav class="st-clock" aria-label="Moments in the day">
        <button type="button" class="st-stop on" aria-pressed="true" data-stop="0"><b>9:02</b>Which terminal?</button>
        <button type="button" class="st-stop" aria-pressed="false" data-stop="1"><b>9:20</b>Port roulette</button>
        <button type="button" class="st-stop" aria-pressed="false" data-stop="2"><b>10:05</b>The fan</button>
        <button type="button" class="st-stop" aria-pressed="false" data-stop="3"><b>11:30</b>Ask the AI</button>
        <button type="button" class="st-stop" aria-pressed="false" data-stop="4"><b>14:00</b>Back after months</button>
        <button type="button" class="st-stop" aria-pressed="false" data-stop="5"><b>18:40</b>Close the lid</button>
        <button type="button" class="st-stop" aria-pressed="false" data-stop="6"><b>19:00</b>The same day, twice</button>
    </nav>

    <div class="st-w" data-day>
      <div class="st-s6">
        <div class="st-seg" role="group" aria-label="How it is, or with doze">
          <button type="button" class="on" aria-pressed="true" data-act="before">How it is</button>
          <button type="button" class="d" aria-pressed="false" data-act="doze">With doze</button>
        </div>
        <div class="st-nav">
          <button type="button" data-act="prev" aria-label="Earlier in the day">← Earlier</button>
          <button type="button" class="go" data-act="next">Now with doze →</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="st-w" data-scene="0">
        <div class="st-scene">
          <div class="st-tell">
            <span class="st-time">9:02</span>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before">
              <h2>Which terminal was that?</h2>
              <p>Coffee. Laptop open. Seven tabs from yesterday, and you don't know which ones are still running.</p><p>The web app starts from package.json. The API from pyproject.toml. The worker is a go run. The database is docker compose. Kafka is a script that needs a different Java. The README explains four of these.</p>
              <p class="st-jab">You didn't design this. It grew.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden>
              <h2 class="st-calm">One file. One command.</h2>
              <p>The commands didn't go anywhere. They live in doze.hcl, the way you already type them, and doze starts them in the right order with the right addresses.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="st-show">
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before"><div class="st-mess">
<div class="st-tabs"><span class="st-tab">web · pnpm dev</span><span class="st-tab on">api · poetry run…</span><span class="st-tab">worker · go run</span><span class="st-tab">docker compose</span><span class="st-tab">kafka.sh</span><span class="st-tab">zsh</span><span class="st-tab">zsh (??)</span></div>

<div class="st-win"><div class="st-bar"><i class="st-s7"></i><i class="st-s8"></i><i class="st-s9"></i><span>api — zsh</span></div><pre class="st-pre st-s10"><span class="st-dim">$</span> poetry run uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
<span class="st-bad">ERROR:    [Errno 48] Address already in use</span>
<span class="st-dim">$</span> # was it 8000 or 8001 for this one</pre></div>
<div class="st-files"><div class="st-file"><b>package.json</b><span>"dev": "vite --port 3001"</span></div><div class="st-file"><b>pyproject.toml</b><span>[tool.poetry.scripts]</span></div><div class="st-file"><b>Makefile</b><span>dev: ## TODO</span></div><div class="st-file"><b>docker-compose.yml</b><span>postgres, redis</span></div><div class="st-file"><b>docker-compose.override.yml</b><span>yours, not committed</span></div><div class="st-file"><b>Procfile.dev</b><span>nobody uses this</span></div><div class="st-file"><b>.env</b><span>DATABASE_URL=…5432</span></div><div class="st-file"><b>.env.local</b><span>DATABASE_URL=…5433</span></div><div class="st-file"><b>README.md</b><span>Getting started (2023)</span></div></div></div></div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden><div class="st-calmbox">

<div class="st-win"><div class="st-bar"><i class="st-s7"></i><i class="st-s8"></i><i class="st-s9"></i><span>larder — zsh</span></div><pre class="st-pre st-s10"><span class="st-dim">$</span> doze up
<span class="st-ok">✓</span> postgres     <span class="st-dim">asleep · wakes on the first connection</span>
<span class="st-ok">✓</span> kafka        <span class="st-dim">asleep · wakes on the first connection</span>
<span class="st-ok">✓</span> migrate-orders <span class="st-dim">done · 2 files</span>
<span class="st-ok">✓</span> gateway      <span class="st-amb">http://gateway.larder.doze</span>
<span class="st-ok">✓</span> storefront   <span class="st-amb">http://storefront.larder.doze</span>
<span class="st-ok">✓</span> fulfilment   <span class="st-dim">awake · uv run python -m fulfilment</span>
<span class="st-dim">  9 apps, 4 modules, 1 service from doze.hcl</span></pre></div>
<pre class="st-code"><span class="st-k">app</span> <span class="st-s">"storefront"</span> &#123; run = <span class="st-s">"bun run dev"</span> &#125;
<span class="st-k">app</span> <span class="st-s">"recommendations"</span> &#123; run = <span class="st-s">"uv run python -m recommendations"</span> &#125;
<span class="st-k">app</span> <span class="st-s">"orders"</span> &#123; run = <span class="st-s">"go run ./services/orders"</span> &#125;</pre></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="st-w" data-scene="1" hidden>
        <div class="st-scene">
          <div class="st-tell">
            <span class="st-time">9:20</span>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before">
              <h2>Port roulette.</h2>
              <p>Address already in use. Something has 8000. You check: it's Python. Which Python?</p><p>And 5432 is a Postgres, but not this project's. It's the one from the client thing last week, still up, holding the port with the wrong data in it.</p>
              <p class="st-jab">You keep the ports in your head. Your head is full.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden>
              <h2 class="st-calm">Names, not numbers. And it tells you who's in the way.</h2>
              <p>Every service gets a name of its own, so two projects can both use 5432 without a clash. When a port is taken, doze says who holds it and offers to move them.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="st-show">
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before"><div class="st-mess">

<div class="st-win"><div class="st-bar"><i class="st-s7"></i><i class="st-s8"></i><i class="st-s9"></i><span>zsh</span></div><pre class="st-pre st-s10"><span class="st-dim">$</span> lsof -i :5432
COMMAND   PID USER  NAME
postgres 4121 you   localhost:postgresql (LISTEN)
<span class="st-dim">$</span> # …which project is that
<span class="st-dim">$</span> lsof -i :8000
python3  5387 you   *:irdmi (LISTEN)</pre></div>
<div class="st-ports"><div class="st-port"><b>:3000</b><span>web?</span></div><div class="st-port"><b>:3001</b><span>the other web</span></div><div class="st-port"><b>:5173</b><span>vite, somewhere</span></div><div class="st-port"><b>:8000</b><span>api (or billing)</span></div><div class="st-port"><b>:8080</b><span>???</span></div><div class="st-port"><b>:5432</b><span>db (which?)</span></div><div class="st-port"><b>:5433</b><span>db, project 2</span></div><div class="st-port"><b>:6379</b><span>redis, shared?</span></div></div></div></div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden><div class="st-calmbox">
<div class="st-names"><div class="st-name"><i></i><b>storefront</b><code>http://storefront.larder.doze</code></div><div class="st-name"><i></i><b>gateway</b><code>http://gateway.larder.doze</code></div><div class="st-name"><i></i><b>postgres</b><code>postgres.larder.doze:5432</code></div><div class="st-name"><i></i><b>postgres</b><code>postgres.billing.doze:5432</code></div></div>

<div class="st-win"><div class="st-bar"><i class="st-s7"></i><i class="st-s8"></i><i class="st-s9"></i><span>larder — zsh</span></div><pre class="st-pre st-s10"><span class="st-dim">$</span> doze up
<span class="st-bad">✗</span> gateway  port 8000 is taken
    held by python3 (pid 5387) on 127.0.0.1:8000
    <span class="st-dim">from ~/code/billing · stop it, or give gateway another port</span></pre></div></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="st-w" data-scene="2" hidden>
        <div class="st-scene">
          <div class="st-tell">
            <span class="st-time">10:05</span>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before">
              <h2>The fan.</h2>
              <p>You're reading code. Nothing is running a test. The fan is.</p><p>A VM is holding every database you've ever started, all day, whether anything talks to it or not. Your battery knows. Your lap knows.</p>
              <p class="st-jab">Open Activity Monitor. We'll wait. We won't make up your numbers for you.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden>
              <h2 class="st-calm">Asleep means asleep.</h2>
              <p>No VM. Real processes, started when something connects and stopped two minutes after nothing does. The data stays on disk. Go and look: there's nothing there.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="st-show">
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before"><div class="st-mess">
<div class="st-am">
  <div class="st-am-h"><b>Activity Monitor</b><span>Memory</span></div>
  <div class="st-am-r hot"><span>Docker Desktop · VM</span><b>[your GB]</b></div><div class="st-am-r"><span>com.docker.backend</span><b>[your MB]</b></div><div class="st-am-r"><span>postgres (container)</span><b>[running since Friday]</b></div><div class="st-am-r"><span>redis (container)</span><b>[running since Friday]</b></div><div class="st-am-r"><span>kafka (container, JVM)</span><b>[your GB]</b></div><div class="st-am-r"><span>node · vite</span><b>[yours]</b></div>
</div>
<div class="st-heat"><span>Fan</span><div><i class="st-s11"></i></div><span>Battery</span><div><i class="st-s12"></i></div></div></div></div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden><div class="st-calmbox">

<div class="st-win"><div class="st-bar"><i class="st-s7"></i><i class="st-s8"></i><i class="st-s9"></i><span>larder — zsh</span></div><pre class="st-pre st-s10"><span class="st-dim">$</span> doze status
  <span class="st-dim">○</span> postgres   asleep <span class="st-dim">· wakes on a connection</span>
  <span class="st-dim">○</span> redis      asleep <span class="st-dim">· wakes on a connection</span>
  <span class="st-dim">○</span> kafka      asleep <span class="st-dim">· wakes on a connection</span>
  <span class="st-ok">●</span> gateway    awake  <span class="st-dim">· sleeps in 1:40</span>
<span class="st-dim">$</span> pgrep -l postgres
<span class="st-dim"># nothing. it's asleep.</span></pre></div></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="st-w" data-scene="3" hidden>
        <div class="st-scene">
          <div class="st-tell">
            <span class="st-time">11:30</span>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before">
              <h2>Ask the AI.</h2>
              <p>Orders can't reach the database. You ask your agent. It's quick, confident, and wrong.</p><p>It read every file in the repo. It still can't see your machine: which compose file is up, what's on which port, what you started yesterday and forgot.</p>
              <p class="st-jab">It isn't stupid. Nobody told it what's running.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden>
              <h2 class="st-calm">Give it the truth, not a guess.</h2>
              <p>doze knows what's running, where, and why it stopped. Your agent asks doze instead of guessing from files: doze status --json is the same answer, for machines.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="st-show">
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before"><div class="st-mess">
<div class="st-chat">
  <div class="st-me">orders can't reach the database. fix it?</div>
  <div class="st-ai">Make sure Postgres is running on <code>localhost:5432</code> and that <code>DATABASE_URL</code> is set in your .env file.</div>
  <div class="st-me">it is. it's… a different project's postgres</div>
  <div class="st-ai">Apologies for the confusion! Try port <code>5433</code>.</div>
  <div class="st-me">that's the other other one</div>
</div></div></div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden><div class="st-calmbox">

<div class="st-win"><div class="st-bar"><i class="st-s7"></i><i class="st-s8"></i><i class="st-s9"></i><span>agent — zsh</span></div><pre class="st-pre st-s10"><span class="st-dim">$</span> doze status
  <span class="st-ok">●</span> postgres  awake  <span class="st-dim">postgres.larder.doze:5432</span>
  <span class="st-bad">●</span> orders    crashing <span class="st-dim">· try 2 of 5</span>
      <span class="st-bad">password authentication failed for user "orders"</span></pre></div>
<div class="st-chat">
  <div class="st-ai">orders is crashing on a password: <code>.env.local</code> overrides the <code>DATABASE_URL</code> doze gives it. Remove that line?</div>
</div></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="st-w" data-scene="4" hidden>
        <div class="st-scene">
          <div class="st-tell">
            <span class="st-time">14:00</span>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before">
              <h2>Back after six months.</h2>
              <p>Someone needs a fix in a repo you haven't opened since spring. You know this one. You wrote half of it.</p><p>make dev is gone. There's a TypeScript service you've never seen. .env.example is three variables short. Nothing is wrong, exactly. It just isn't familiar any more.</p>
              <p class="st-jab">The setup doc rots the day after someone writes it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden>
              <h2 class="st-calm">The file that runs the stack can't go stale.</h2>
              <p>If doze.hcl is wrong, nothing starts, so it never drifts from the truth. Pull, doze up, and the new service is simply there, wired to what it needs.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="st-show">
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before"><div class="st-mess">

<div class="st-win"><div class="st-bar"><i class="st-s7"></i><i class="st-s8"></i><i class="st-s9"></i><span>billing — zsh</span></div><pre class="st-pre st-s10"><span class="st-dim">$</span> make dev
<span class="st-bad">make: *** No rule to make target 'dev'.  Stop.</span>
<span class="st-dim">$</span> git log --oneline -3 -- services/
a41c9e0 add notifications service (TypeScript)
7be20d1 move worker to Python
19ff3a2 bump node to 22</pre></div>
<div class="st-readme"><b>README.md</b><s>1. make dev</s><s>2. open localhost:3000</s><span>3. ask Priya</span></div></div></div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden><div class="st-calmbox">

<div class="st-win"><div class="st-bar"><i class="st-s7"></i><i class="st-s8"></i><i class="st-s9"></i><span>billing — zsh</span></div><pre class="st-pre st-s10"><span class="st-dim">$</span> git pull && doze up
<span class="st-ok">✓</span> install-notifications <span class="st-dim">done · bun install (lockfile changed)</span>
<span class="st-ok">✓</span> notifications         awake</pre></div>
<pre class="st-code"><span class="st-add">+ app "notifications" &#123;
+   dir = "services/notifications"
+   run = "bun src/index.ts"
+   env = &#123; KAFKA_BROKERS = module.kafka.address &#125;
+ &#125;</span></pre></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="st-w" data-scene="5" hidden>
        <div class="st-scene">
          <div class="st-tell">
            <span class="st-time">18:40</span>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before">
              <h2>Close the lid.</h2>
              <p>Done for the day. Lid shut, bag zipped.</p><p>Twenty-three containers from three projects are still up. Two node processes have been running since yesterday. The bag is warm by the time you're home.</p>
              <p class="st-jab">Nothing stops on its own. So nothing stops.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden>
              <h2 class="st-calm">It goes to sleep. So can you.</h2>
              <p>Every stack, in the menu bar. Idle services are already asleep; quit the app and your stacks keep running, asleep, until something calls them in the morning.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="st-show">
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="before"><div class="st-mess">

<div class="st-win"><div class="st-bar"><i class="st-s7"></i><i class="st-s8"></i><i class="st-s9"></i><span>zsh</span></div><pre class="st-pre st-s10"><span class="st-dim">$</span> docker ps --format '&#123;&#123;.Names&#125;&#125;' | wc -l
      23
<span class="st-dim">$</span> ps -eo etime,comm | grep node
 1-02:14:09 node
 1-01:58:40 node</pre></div></div></div>
            <div class="st-w" data-mode="doze" hidden><div class="st-calmbox">
<div class="st-menu">
  <div class="st-menu-h">Stacks</div>
  <div class="st-menu-r on"><span><i class="st-s13"></i>larder</span><b>all asleep</b></div>
  <div class="st-menu-r"><span><i class="st-s13"></i>billing</span><b>all asleep</b></div>
  <div class="st-menu-r"><span><i class="st-s14"></i>acme</span><b>down</b></div>
  <div class="st-menu-sep"></div>
  <div class="st-menu-r"><span>Quit doze</span><b>stacks keep running</b></div>
</div></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="st-s15">
        <span class="st-eyebrow st-s16" data-meter-title>The mess meter, so far today</span>
        <div class="st-meter" role="status" aria-live="polite">
            <div class="st-m"><b class="st-m-bad">7</b><span>commands to remember</span><small></small></div>
            <div class="st-m"><b class="st-m-zero">0</b><span>ports to keep in your head</span><small></small></div>
            <div class="st-m"><b class="st-m-bad">9</b><span>files to read before you start</span><small></small></div>
            <div class="st-m"><b class="st-m-zero">0</b><span>still running when you close the lid</span><small></small></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="st-w" data-end hidden>
      <div class="st-s17">
        <h2 class="st-h st-s18" tabindex="-1" data-end-title>The same Tuesday, twice.</h2>
        <div class="st-sum">
          <div class="st-col st-s19">
            <b class="st-s20">How it is</b>
            <div class="st-row"><span class="st-s21">commands to remember</span><b class="st-s22">7</b></div>
            <div class="st-row"><span class="st-s21">ports to keep in your head</span><b class="st-s22">8</b></div>
            <div class="st-row"><span class="st-s21">files to read before you start</span><b class="st-s22">9</b></div>
            <div class="st-row"><span class="st-s21">still running when you close the lid</span><b class="st-s22">23</b></div>
          </div>
          <div class="st-col st-s23">
            <b class="st-s24">With doze</b>
            <div class="st-row"><span class="st-s25">commands to remember <small class="st-s26">· doze up</small></span><b class="st-s27">1</b></div>
            <div class="st-row"><span class="st-s25">ports to keep in your head <small class="st-s26">· every service has a name</small></span><b class="st-s27">0</b></div>
            <div class="st-row"><span class="st-s25">files to read before you start <small class="st-s26">· doze.hcl</small></span><b class="st-s27">1</b></div>
            <div class="st-row"><span class="st-s25">still running when you close the lid <small class="st-s26">· everything idle is asleep</small></span><b class="st-s27">0</b></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="st-s28">This Tuesday is a story, and its counts are the story's. Yours will differ. That's rather the point: count yours.</p>
        <div class="st-s29">
          <a class="st-s30" href="/download/">Get doze</a>
          <a class="st-s31" href="/examples/">Run Larder: a whole stack, one command</a>
          <button class="st-s32" type="button" data-act="restart">Start the day again</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</Page>

<script>import "../scripts/story-tuesday.ts";</script>

<style>
.st a{color:#F0A24B;text-decoration:none}
.st-eyebrow{font:13px var(--font-mono);letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#F0A24B}
.st-h{margin:0;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.035em;line-height:.98;text-wrap:balance}
.st-clock{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(7,minmax(0,1fr));gap:8px;position:relative}
.st-stop{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;align-items:flex-start;text-align:left;padding:14px 14px 12px;border-radius:14px;border:1px solid #34233F;background:#1A1022;color:#C9BAD3;font:500 14px var(--font-text);cursor:pointer;min-height:76px}
.st-stop b{font:600 20px var(--font-mono);color:#F4ECE4}
.st-stop:hover{border-color:#7A5E8C}
.st-stop.on{border-color:#F0A24B;background:#2A1A34;box-shadow:0 0 0 1px #F0A24B}
.st-stop.done b{color:#9C8AAB}
.st-stop:focus-visible,.st-seg button:focus-visible,.st-nav button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #F0A24B;outline-offset:2px}
.st-seg{display:inline-flex;padding:4px;border-radius:12px;background:#1A1022;border:1px solid #34233F}
.st-seg button{height:44px;padding:0 18px;border-radius:9px;border:0;background:transparent;color:#C9BAD3;font:600 15px var(--font-text);cursor:pointer}
.st-seg button.on{background:#F4ECE4;color:#140C1B}
.st-seg button.on.d{background:#F0A24B;color:#2A1534}
.st-scene{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,5fr) minmax(0,7fr);gap:48px;align-items:start}
